; Oasis prefs: copy this file to S:Oasis.prefs, or keep it next to Oasis.
; Lines starting with ; are comments. After editing, choose Project > Reload prefs.
;
; LEFT and RIGHT: the drawers the panes open on ("" = the device list).
;LEFT "Work:"
;RIGHT ""
;
; SORT NAME, SIZE or DATE.  HIDEICONS YES hides the .info files.
SORT NAME
HIDEICONS NO
;
; Custom buttons (up to 12), shown in a row under the others:
;   BUTTON "Label" [QUIET] command line
; In the command, %s is the selected files (quoted full paths), %f the first of them,
; %p the drawer they are in, %d the drawer in the other pane, %% a percent sign.
; The output appears in a window that waits for Return; QUIET throws it away (use
; QUIET with Run for programs that open their own window).
BUTTON "Read" Type %f
BUTTON "Edit" QUIET Run Ed %f
BUTTON "Notepad" QUIET Run SYS:Utilities/NotePad %f
BUTTON "List" List %p
BUTTON "Disks" Info
BUTTON "Memory" Avail
